{
 "id": "mms_stokes_axi",
 "capability": "F1b",
 "title": "Axisymmetric MMS with swirl, all-Dirichlet + axis, both viscous forms, variable mu, two mesh families",
 "physics": "u_r, u_theta odd and u_z, p, mu even in r; Dirichlet on r = 1, z = 0, z = 1 (u.n != 0); axis r = 0",
 "levels": [
  "mms"
 ],
 "run": {
  "runner": {
   "module": "f1b_stokes",
   "function": "mms_dirichlet",
   "check_module": "f1b_stokes_check",
   "cost": "long",
   "timeout_s": 7200
  },
  "parameters": {
   "element": {
    "velocity": "P2 (u_r, u_z, u_theta)",
    "pressure": "P1",
    "geometry": "affine"
   },
   "formulation": "weight r in every volume and boundary integral; continuity tested with r q (symmetric saddle point); grad u with the hoop entries (r,theta) = -u_theta/r, (theta,theta) = u_r/r; lap a = int mu grad u : grad v r, sym a = int 2 mu eps(u) : eps(v) r; traction g = sigma_form n (vector (g_r, g_z, g_theta)); grad-div gamma (div_r u, div_r v)_r with div_r u = d_r u_r + u_r/r + d_z u_z, the weight r, gamma in viscosity units (tools/fluids_mms/axi_stokes.py docstring)",
   "forms": [
    "lap",
    "sym"
   ],
   "quadrature_error_norms": 10,
   "solver": {
    "kind": "direct sparse LU",
    "tight": "same, plus 2 steps of iterative refinement (vacuous for a direct solve; meaningful for an iterative path)"
   },
   "axis_rule": "Axis r = 0 (attribute 'axis'): u_r = u_theta = 0 STRONGLY at every P2 velocity node on the axis (vertices and edge nodes), rows and columns eliminated (the assembled axis-axis entries are never used); u_z and p natural. No quadrature point on r = 0 (the hoop integrands u v / r are rational on elements that touch the axis at one vertex).",
   "shared_node_rule": "At a velocity node shared by several boundary attributes: (1) Dirichlet beats every natural condition and the axis condition (the fixed data satisfy u_r = u_theta = 0 at r = 0 anyway); (2) between Dirichlet attributes the fixed data AGREE at shared nodes (one exact callable per field: checked by dirichlet_shared_node_mismatch_max), so the result does not depend on attribute order; (3) a node shared by the axis and a natural (traction / do-nothing) attribute takes the axis condition u_r = u_theta = 0 (strong) and the natural condition for u_z.",
   "dirichlet_data": "Dirichlet data by P2 LAGRANGE NODAL INTERPOLATION of the fixed callable (exact at vertices and edge nodes); checked on the solution by dirichlet_nodal_data_defect_max.",
   "quadrature": "QUADRATURE REQUIREMENTS: (a) no quadrature point on r = 0; (b) the viscous rule (including the 1/r hoop terms) and the load rule exact to degree >= 4 on affine elements (the order-4 functionals need it; degree 3 drops the torque orders to 2.96); (c) the continuity / pressure coupling (div_r v, q)_r integrated exactly, i.e. degree >= 3 on affine elements; (d) grad-div assembled with the SAME rule as the viscous 1/r terms. The constant-mu identity and continuity_rq_max_rel hold to round-off only under (c) and (d) (measured: a degree-2 grad-div rule gives identity p 5e-7, a degree-2 (div, q) rule continuity 3e-5).",
   "mms_data": {
    "path": "tools/fluids_mms/out/f1b/axi_dirichlet.json",
